  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, the family home is deductible from the gross estate, with a maximum deduction of up to P10 million.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nThe deduction for the family home is significant for estate planning and tax purposes, as it allows families to retain a larger portion of their assets after the death of a family member. By deducting the value of the family home, heirs can minimize the estate tax burden, ensuring that more of the estate is preserved for the beneficiaries.",
